.TH FPUTS 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fputs \- write a string to a Crunch stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int fputs(const char* " text ", struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes the NUL-terminated string without writing the terminating NUL or adding
a newline. An empty string succeeds without writing.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a nonnegative value on success or
.B EOF
(\-1) on error. An I/O error sets
.B errno
and the stream error indicator; some bytes may already have been written.
A null string or stream fails with
.BR EINVAL ;
when the stream is valid its error indicator is set.
.SH NOTES
I/O is unbuffered. Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fgets (3crunch),
.BR fputc (3crunch),
.BR fwrite (3crunch),
.BR ferror (3crunch)
